/** @mainpage

This suite exercises tsf-ics - talking to an industrial control device
(Modbus TCP) from the Test Agent it runs on, over libmodbus:

- @ref ics-read - read holding and input registers and coils/discrete
  inputs from an endpoint, and a device identification;
- @ref ics-audit - read the endpoint as a security posture through
  tsf-cybersec: Modbus has no authentication, so a reachable endpoint
  answers anyone - a readable area, a device-id fingerprint, and (only
  when explicitly enabled and done reversibly) a writable register.

There is no Modbus device on a stock host, so both tests SKIP cleanly
unless an endpoint is configured through the TSF_ICS_HOST / TSF_ICS_PORT
/ TSF_ICS_UNIT environment variables; the write probe stays off unless
TSF_ICS_WRITE=1. The point is that tsf-ics drives Modbus over the
library (not by scraping a tool) and turns an unauthenticated control
surface into findings. Authorized use only - a configured endpoint must
be a device you own or are engaged to test.

*/
